From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
Subject: [PATCH 1/2] glsl: pass vulkan_lib_dirs to find_library('glslang')

The static `cxx.find_library` for the SPIRV/MachineIndependent/OSDependent/
GenericCodeGen sub-archives all pass `dirs: vulkan_lib_dirs` so they pick
up the glslang install in `<vulkan-sdk>/lib`. The find_library for
`glslang` itself was missed and only searches the C++ compiler's default
library path.

In a cross-compile setup (e.g. iOS-on-MoltenVK), the toolchain's lib path
doesn't contain anything we install ourselves, so the lookup fails with
"C++ static library 'glslang' not found" even though the install is
correct.

Mirror the sibling lookups: pass `dirs: vulkan_lib_dirs`.
---
 src/glsl/meson.build | 2 +-
 1 file changed, 1 insertion(+), 1 deletion(-)

diff --git a/src/glsl/meson.build b/src/glsl/meson.build
index c9a8542..95aac1a 100644
--- a/src/glsl/meson.build
+++ b/src/glsl/meson.build
@@ -59,7 +59,7 @@ elif not glslang_req.disabled()

     # Glslang 15.0.0 moved some code around, add also linking to glslang, while
     # this is not needed for older versions, it will still work.
-    glslang_deps += cxx.find_library('glslang', required: required, static: static)
+    glslang_deps += cxx.find_library('glslang', required: required, static: static, dirs: vulkan_lib_dirs)

     if static
       glslang_deps += [
